# Keep Go sources LF in the working tree regardless of core.autocrlf, so gofmt and
# the gofmt linter see the same LF the repo already stores. Without this, a CRLF
# checkout (autocrlf=true on Windows) makes `gofmt -l` flag every file even though
# the committed source is clean. Other paths keep git's default handling.
*.go text eol=lf

# Vendored vocabulary glyphs are byte copies of the contracts catalog, pinned by SHA-256 in
# assets/glyphs/PROVENANCE.txt - never let a checkout rewrite their line endings.
assets/glyphs/*.svg -text

# The SZA web kit is a byte copy of the contracts catalog reference (PAGE-STYLE), pinned by SHA-256
# in tests/site_test.go - page-local rules live in assets/site.css, never in the kit.
assets/sza-kit.css -text

# The bundled pdftotext set is byte copies of upstream binaries, pinned by SHA-256 in
# internal/bundledtools/PROVENANCE.txt - never let a checkout rewrite them.
internal/bundledtools/pdftotext/* -text

# The in-app help set (ticket 118) is generated by tools/helpgen and embedded byte for byte; its mirror under help/ is
# published from the same bytes. The vendored help.css is a byte copy of the contracts catalog reference. Never let a
# checkout rewrite their line endings.
cmd/doc-html-ui/help/** -text
help/** -text
tools/helpgen/vendor/* -text

# The Partner Center listing export and its emptied-copy fixture are in the export's own dialect (UTF-8 BOM, CRLF
# between records, LF inside cells, no trailing newline). The builder writes that dialect and refuses any other, and
# proves itself with a byte-identical -FillNothing round trip (WINDOWS-STORE rules 8 and 13) - never let a checkout
# rewrite their line endings.
tools/store/listingData.csv -text
tools/store/listingData.sample.csv -text
